urname>Lauvrak</surname><given-names>SU</given-names></name><name><surname>Torgersen</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Iversen</surname><given-names>TG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Pathways followed by protein toxins into cells.</article-title><source>Int J Med Microbiol</source><volume>293</volume><fpage>483</fpage><lpage>490</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15149022</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002933-Smith1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lord</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Roberts</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Johannes</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Glycosphingolipids as toxin receptors.</article-title><source>Semin Cell Dev Biol</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>397</fpage><lpage>408</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15207830</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002933-Yanagisawa1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yanagisawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Odaka</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Suzuki</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Ihara</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>GM1 ganglioside-bound amyloid beta-protein (A beta): a possible form of preamyloid in Alzheimer's disease.</article-title><source>Nat Med</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>1062</fpage><lpage>1066</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7489364</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002933-Mahfoud1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mahfoud</surname><given-names>R</given-names></na